<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Melee. Color + Eltex. The grip is lined with lead, a psychically inert
       lining: the eltex pair's mirror, and the first wielder-side malus that is still a weapon stat.
       INTENT: "a weapon that deadens its wielder's psychic sensitivity, for better and for worse."
       Routing: Core's PsychicSensitivity carries StatPart_GearStatFactor with includeWeapon, which
       reads the primary weapon's PsychicSensitivityFactor as a weapon-thing stat;
       CompUniqueWeapon.GetStatFactor hands it this trait's statFactors and the pawn's breakdown
       lists the weapon under "Relevant gear". No hediff, no patch, no TraitEffectSummary case.
       Mass, cooldown and market value are ordinary weapon stats, as on UMW_Cumbersome. Not
       quality-scaled: the factor has no quality part, so every value here is flat.
       Two-sided by design: the x0.9 that weakens a psycaster is also a shield against psychic
       drones, shock and insanity lances and soothe/insanity events. The description states only the
       suppression, as vanilla's psychic quiet does; the sensitivity stat tooltip explains the two sides.
       Anchors: mass x1.1 and cooldown x1.05 sit under Cumbersome's x1.3 / x1.15 (the weight is a
       side effect of the lining); MarketValue x0.9 follows the MV rule (devaluation is a factor),
       a lighter touch than Ugly's and Cumbersome's x0.8 because the effect cuts both ways. Under
       Combat Extended the Mass factor is mirrored onto CE's Bulk
       (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/WeaponTraits_CE.xml).
       Tokens: Color (it forces Odyssey's UniqueWeapon_Gray onto colour one via vanilla forcedColor,
       so it excludes the inlays, Envenomed, ZeusHeaded and UMW_EltexFitted) and Eltex (so a plated
       weapon is never also lead-lined). NO Weight token: the lining is not the Weight axis, and a
       light blade with a leaden grip reads fine (Lightweight 0.7 x 1.1 nets 0.77 mass; Cumbersome
       1.3 x 1.1 nets 1.43, acceptable).
       Colour: UniqueWeapon_Gray (100, 100, 100) reused by decision rather than a sixth ColorDef;
       it is in Odyssey's random accent pool, so a plain weapon can roll the same grey and the trait
       line is the tell, as for every stat-only trait. UniqueWeapon_Black was rejected as reading
       like Carbon black.
       Root: the factor would work without Royalty (drones and lances are Core), but it is only
       legible beside the psychic system, and keeping it out of the ungated tree leaves Royalty-less
       games with the core pool's negative skew unchanged. Period-neutral, so the war merchant's
       ultratech ban does not name it. canGenerateAlone false with a MarketValue factor, the
       project's malus signal (Ugly, Cumbersome); commonality 0.5, the Royalty root's rarer tier, so
       it stays a surprise rather than a tax. -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_LeadLined</defName>
    <label>lead-lined</label>
    <description>The grip is lined with lead, which suppresses the wielder's psychic sensitivity. The extra weight slows the swing.</description>
    <commonality>0.5</commonality>
    <canGenerateAlone>false</canGenerateAlone>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Melee</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Color</li>
      <li>Eltex</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <forcedColor>UniqueWeapon_Gray</forcedColor> <!-- Odyssey's (100, 100, 100); no new ColorDef -->
    <statFactors>
      <PsychicSensitivityFactor>0.9</PsychicSensitivityFactor> <!-- the malus, and a shield against drones and lances -->
      <Mass>1.1</Mass> <!-- Cumbersome 1.3; the CE root mirrors it onto Bulk -->
      <MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier>1.05</MeleeWeapon_CooldownMultiplier> <!-- Cumbersome 1.15 -->
      <MarketValue>0.9</MarketValue> <!-- devaluation is a factor (MV rule); Ugly/Cumbersome 0.8 -->
    </statFactors>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>lead-lined</li>
      <li>leaden</li>
      <li>deadened</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
